# Autonomous Next-Generation Flexure-Based Alignment and Exposure Stage

## 📌 Project Executive Summary
This repository contains the complete design blueprint, engineering metrics, and control logic for an **autonomous, 3D-printable micro-positioning and exposure system** engineered for photolithography applications. 

By replacing traditional friction-heavy mechanical bearings with compliant monolithic flexure mechanisms, this system completely eliminates backlash and stick-slip friction. The architecture delivers a highly repeatable **5µm alignment resolution** within a tightly constrained **5mm maximum travel envelope**. 

This project demonstrates cross-disciplinary expertise across precision mechatronics, compliant mechanism kinematics, additive manufacturing optimization, and automated system control.

---

## 🛠️ Core Engineering Logic & Subsystems

*   **Compliant Mechanism Kinematics:** Designed custom flexure geometries to guide precision motion. Utilizing structural elasticity allows the system to achieve sub-micron predictability and a **5µm alignment resolution** without the need for high-cost linear guides.
*   **Workspace & Stress Optimization:** Engineered the flexure arms to maximize compliance along the desired axis while ensuring the material stays safely below its yield and fatigue limits during the full **5mm allowed travel distance**.
*   **Additive Manufacturing Integration:** Optimized the entire mechanical assembly for monolithic, **3D-printable manufacturing** (FDM/SLA). The design features print-in-place tolerances that minimize assembly stack-up errors and reduce physical production costs.
*   **Automated Optical Alignment Pipeline:** Developed an autonomous control loop using MATLAB scripts that seamlessly handle the transition from precision structural alignment to timed UV exposure, minimizing human error and maximizing process reliability.

